  "description": "New to the Market \nACRES WOOD\nBallyglass East, Loughglynn, Co. Roscommon\nF45 VF66\n\n3 BEDROOM DETACHED RESIDENCE ON c.0.8 ACRES\n\nGuide Price: €220,000\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers are delighted to bring to the market Acres Wood, an attractive three-bedroom detached residence situated at Ballyglass East, Loughglynn, Co. Roscommon.\n\nSet on approximately 0.8 acres of mature grounds, the property is approached by a long private driveway and enjoys a peaceful countryside setting with an abundance of mature trees and excellent privacy.\n\nThe residence offers spacious accommodation with plenty of traditional character and provides an excellent opportunity for a purchaser seeking a country home with generous outdoor space and useful outbuildings.\n\nAccommodation includes a kitchen, sitting room with traditional feature fireplace, three bedrooms and bathroom.\n\nExternally, the property is set on mature grounds extending to approximately 0.8 acres. A particular feature is the south-facing rear garden, providing an attractive and private outdoor space.\n\nThe property also benefits from a range of useful outbuildings, including a two-bay open hayshed, additional storage/outbuildings and an enclosed penned area suitable for keeping dogs.\n\nAcres Wood combines the privacy and space of a rural property with convenient access to nearby towns and villages. Loughglynn Village is close by, with Castlerea and Ballaghaderreen also within convenient driving distance, while Ireland West Airport Knock is readily accessible.\n\nFEATURES\n\n• Three-bedroom detached residence\n• Set on approximately 0.8 acres\n• Long private driveway\n• Mature gardens and trees\n• Private countryside setting\n• South-facing rear garden\n• Two-bay open hayshed\n• Additional outbuildings\n• Enclosed penned area suitable for dogs\n• Traditional feature fireplace\n• Excellent potential to further enhance\n• Close to Loughglynn Village\n• Convenient to Castlerea and Ballaghaderreen\n• Accessible to Ireland West Airport Knock\n• Eircode: F45 VF66\n\nGUIDE PRICE: €220,000\n\nVIEWING\n\nViewing is strictly by appointment with the Sole Selling Agents:\n\nNigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers\n\nEverything we touch turns to SOLD.\n\nSOLE SELLING AGENT\n\nDISCLAIMER\n\nThese particulars are issued by Nigel Dineen & Martin Finn Auctioneers on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through them. While every care has been taken in preparing these particulars, they are for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. Measurements, areas and distances are approximate, and intending purchasers should satisfy themselves as to the accuracy of all information provided.",
